# Celery

- Keep tasks small and place reusable business logic in services.
- Pass stable IDs instead of model objects or large payloads.
- Make tasks safe for retries and duplicate execution where needed.
- Retry only transient failures and use bounded retry settings.
- Dispatch tasks after required database transactions commit.
- Check schedules, queue routing, Redis usage, and task callers before changes.
